# Copy these site settings into .env. Preserve any credentials already there.
# Values are literal: no shell commands or ${VARIABLE} expansion.
# Exported environment variables override this file. DGPP_ENV_FILE selects
# another file; otherwise scripts find .env at the repository/release root.

# Rank order: each deployment uses the first world_size nodes.
# SSH/control addresses may be management IPs, fabric IPs, or a mixture.
# Rank 0 must reach each peer over SSH; all peers must reach rank 0's listed IP.
# If only rank 0 has a separate management IP, list fabric IPs for all nodes
# when that is how peers reach rank 0. Its operator login can use the other IP.
# The same interfaces can carry SSH/control traffic and RoCE; select RDMA
# devices/GIDs below. A separate management network is optional.
DGPP_NODES="192.0.2.11 192.0.2.12 192.0.2.13 192.0.2.14"
DGPP_SSH_USER=""

DGPP_HTTP_PORT=18080
DGPP_HTTP_BIND=127.0.0.1
DGPP_FABRIC_PORT=29970
DGPP_JOURNAL_PORT=29971
# Each peer rank's metrics listener (dgpp_rank_* on GET /metrics/prometheus, on
# the rank's node address); 0 or unset = off. Rank 0 reports its own on HTTP.
# DGPP_METRICS_PORT=29972
DGPP_LOG_DIR="~/dgpp/log"
DGPP_STAGE_DIR="/tmp/bus4"
DGPP_RELEASE_DIR="~/dgpp/releases"

# Select a deployment with --config /path/to/cluster_config.json.
# scripts/setup.sh saves its selected deployment here for subsequent commands:
# DGPP_CLUSTER_CONFIG="deploy/cluster_qwen-3.8-flash-next_nvfp4_w1.json"

# Deployment http.bind_host and http.port override the HTTP defaults above.
# Set DGPP_NODES="127.0.0.1" for a single-node deployment.
# Build and dataset paths may be relative to the repository root.
# Leave DGPP_BUILD_DIR unset for separate defaults: build-release for serving
# and packaging, build-ci for testing. Use --bin to deploy a testing binary.
# DGPP_BUILD_DIR="custom-build"
# DGPP_DATA_DIR="data"

# Optional cache paths. ~/ expands separately on each node.
# HF_HOME="~/.cache/huggingface"
# HF_HUB_CACHE="~/.cache/huggingface/hub"
# DGPP_RESIDENT_CACHE_DIR="~/dgpp/resident-cache"

# Multi-node only: discover actual names/IPs with:
# python3 scripts/discover_roce.py --config deploy/cluster_glm-5.3-flash_nvfp4-fp8_w4_mtp1.json
# Omit devices to select active Ethernet RDMA devices automatically.
# Use the same lane order and lane count on every node. Names may differ.
# DGPP_ROCE_DEVICES="rocep1s0f0 roceP2p1s0f0"
# Optional explicit GID indices, one per device; otherwise auto-select RoCE v2.
# DGPP_ROCE_GID_INDICES="3 3"
# Per-node overrides use the exact address/name from DGPP_NODES.
# These are example Spark verbs names, not Linux interface names; use discovery
# output for your hosts. Match corresponding subnets in the same lane order.
# DGPP_NODE_OVERRIDES='{"192.0.2.12":{"DGPP_ROCE_DEVICES":"rocep1s0f0 roceP2p1s0f0","HF_HUB_CACHE":"/srv/models/hub"}}'
# The engine's L2 weight-prefetch knobs reach every rank too (an A/B; default on):
# DGPP_L2_PREFETCH=off
# Startup diagnostics, shared by all ranks or set in DGPP_NODE_OVERRIDES:
# DGPP_LOG_LEVEL=debug
# DGPP_MLOCK=off
# DGPP_MLOCK disables optional mlockall only; the server still raises its soft
# memlock limit to the existing hard limit before CUDA/RDMA initialization.
